course: dictionary
lesson: 5630
title: One word, many meanings: limit
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one the writer means. Limit can be a noun, a name for a thing, or a verb, a doing word. «Before playing any game that costs money, decide your limit and stop when you reach it.» Here your limit is the most money you are allowed to spend.
explain: Limit can also mean the edge or end of a place, like the city limits. Look at the words around it. If the sentence is about money, time, speed or screens, limit probably means the most that is allowed.
explain: As a verb, to limit something means to keep it to a certain amount. «Keep to agreed limits» means stay inside the amount you both agreed on. Put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A limit (noun) is the greatest or smallest amount that is allowed or possible, such as a speed limit.
fact: A limit can also be the edge or end of an area, such as the city limits.
fact: To limit something (verb) means to keep it to a certain amount, such as limit screen time.
fact: «Too much screen time can affect mood and sleep», so keeping to agreed limits is a smart idea.
fact: Off limits means not allowed, and «the sky is the limit» means there is no limit at all.
exercise: «Before playing any game that costs money, decide your limit and stop when you reach it.» In this sentence, what does limit mean? | The name of the game | The edge of the playground | Feeling sad about the game | *The most money you are allowed to spend
exercise: Dad says, «Our family has agreed screen limits.» What do the limits mean here? | Long, happy holidays | Walls around our home | *The amounts of screen time we have agreed to keep to | Brand new phones
exercise: Which phrase means there is no limit at all? | Off limits | Time limit | *The sky is the limit | Within limits
test: Mum says, «Let's limit your gaming to one hour.» What does limit mean in this sentence? | To buy a new game | To forget about games | To make gaming last longer | *To keep gaming to a set amount
test: «We stayed within the limits of the park.» What does within the limits mean? | *Inside the edge of the park | Going very fast | Outside the park | Without any money
exam: In «keep to agreed limits», what does limits mean? | Start a new game | Stay out of the house | Forget about the agreement | *Stay inside the greatest amount that everyone agreed
